  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Using the VCC may be a good way to manage packages for some people, but I think it would be good to also allow users to have VRChat SDK packages in a UPM registry.\n\nUPM registries are essentially just NPM registries. Some users have even created unofficial registries with VRChat packages like this: https://twitter.com/Benaclejames/status/1625570122738896926\n\nThe advantage of using a proper UPM registry is, that packages can be updated right within unity via the built in package manager interface as seen below.\n\nIn combination with [OpenUPM](https://openupm.com/) vrchat could even use other 3rd party dependencies as UPM dependencies instead of including them directly, that may be a bit too complicated though and wouldn't work for anyone, who doesn't use OpenUPM.\n\nEither way,  official.upm.vrchat.com and curated.upm.vrchat.com npm registries with all official and curated packages respectively would be nice. Or all in one, I personally don't care too much about the differentiation.\n\nOther community packages like [VRCFury](https://openupm.com/packages/com.vrcfury.vrcfury/), [Pumkins Avatar Tools](https://openupm.com/packages/io.github.rurre.pumkinsavatartools/), [Gesture Manager](https://openupm.com/packages/vrchat.blackstartx.gesture-manager/), [AudioLink](https://openupm.com/packages/com.llealloo.audiolink/) are already on OpenUPM and can be installed through their Package Registry.",
